+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an array of JSON Patch operations from RFC 6902 and returns a
+new JSON value without changing `document`. It supports `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and
+`test`. Operation paths and `from` paths use JSON Pointer syntax. Array additions may use `-` to
+append; other array indices must be decimal indices without leading zeroes. Invalid operations,
+paths that do not resolve, and failed `test` operations throw an error.
